1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,060
A show at 6-5-6, and we're on the radio!

2
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:08,040
We hope you'll be there.

3
00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:09,700
Thank you.

4
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:13,740
It feels like we're starting to make real progress.

5
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:18,380
The schedule sure is filling up, huh?

6
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:21,720
Half of these dates are for our part-time jobs, but yeah.

7
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:26,420
Hell, if we're paying off our debt and doing idle stuff at the same time, we're on our way to Easy Street.

8
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:28,100
Nope, not even close.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,300
If we start thinking we can relax now, then all we'll ever be known for is the time we bombed.

10
00:00:47,960 --> 00:00:52,600
We need to put the past behind us, find a way to rise above everyone's expectations.

11
00:00:53,460 --> 00:00:56,720
And if we can't, then we might as well be dead and buried.

12
00:00:56,720 --> 00:01:02,480
She's got a point. The entertainment industry's always been a cutthroat competition.

13
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:05,300
And to fall behind is to die.

14
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:17,740
I can't say no to a challenge.

15
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:19,320
Right, let's advance.

16
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:21,340
Better count me and two!

17
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:24,020
Come on, Ty!

18
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:27,280
I's exactly right.

19
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,420
We have to keep growing and moving forward.

20
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:32,740
Thank you for supporting the group!

21
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:35,000
Number three is so inspirational!

22
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:37,680
Yeah, you can tell she puts her all into it!

23
00:01:38,180 --> 00:01:38,500
Question.

24
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:40,140
Which one looks better?

25
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:40,660
Watch.

26
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:43,140
Arm pointed out to the side or kind of downward?

27
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:44,300
Real quick.

28
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:46,680
I put together the intro for tomorrow's show.

29
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:48,040
Could you look it over for me?

30
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:51,720
I can't decide which one of these hair pieces would make me cuter!

31
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:52,740
Let me see here.

32
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:57,480
Either, both, doesn't matter.

33
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:04,900
Ai, can you please tell me what to do?

34
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:06,440
Ai, can I ask you for something?

35
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:08,140
Ai, do you have just a second?

36
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:09,400
Ai, help!

37
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:09,820
Ah!

38
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:12,920
Sakura center.

39
00:02:13,460 --> 00:02:15,380
Junko and Lily, you'll be on the right side.

40
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:17,560
And Saki and Yugiri, you go on the left.

41
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:19,460
Back a bit more.

42
00:02:19,460 --> 00:02:27,080
Iron Frill is coming here.

43
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:29,780
Iron Frill is coming here.

44
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:32,820
So get your zombie butts in here.

45
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:34,560
Let's go!

46
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:35,460
It's a raid!

47
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:36,160
An ambush!

48
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:37,160
They're coming!

49
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:39,460
You little guy!

50
00:02:45,300 --> 00:02:45,940
Inai!

51
00:02:46,220 --> 00:02:48,420
You are to respond with a sir, yes, sir!

52
00:02:48,420 --> 00:02:53,860
You're just a bunch of wet corpses wallowing around in muck!

53
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:57,740
No, you're the maggots that ate the corpses!

54
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,200
Would you calm down?

55
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:00,740
Get back to Iron Frill.

56
00:03:02,380 --> 00:03:05,960
Get the shit out of your ears and listen up, you shamble and sacks of bones!

57
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:10,480
There's about to be another landmark added to the fierce battlefield that is Saga.

58
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:12,420
The new Saga Arena!

59
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:14,040
Wait, the what now?

60
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:16,200
And guess who's breaking it in first?

61
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:17,820
Iron Frill, obviously!

62
00:03:18,540 --> 00:03:18,880
Huh?

63
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:23,180
Now, why is a big-time idol group from Tokyo being brought in for the inaugural performance

64
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:25,260
at a venue in Little Old Saga, you may ask?

65
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:27,620
And to that I say, who freaking knows?

66
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:31,760
The important takeaway is that I found a way to weasel you maggots in as the opening air!

67
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:37,500
You and those are going to be so awesome that those Tokyo are going to leave here not to shame!

68
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:38,760
It's the perfect plan!

69
00:03:38,880 --> 00:03:40,080
So memorize it!

70
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:41,140
You're kidding!

71
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:42,780
The Iron Frill?

72
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:48,880
Good!

73
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:54,000
We can handle this!

74
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:55,700
I know it!

75
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,020
You're right!

76
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:03,440
Yeah, lovely parade and all, but here comes the rain.

77
00:04:03,760 --> 00:04:05,080
Number three's not performing.

78
00:04:05,500 --> 00:04:05,820
What?

79
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:06,540
Why?

80
00:04:06,540 --> 00:04:07,400
Oh?

81
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:09,700
Did all your brains finally leak out?

82
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:14,300
Iron Frill's famously deceased leader wants to flaunt her undeadliness right in front of

83
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:14,920
her old group?

84
00:04:16,060 --> 00:04:20,260
We've been up in Saga's grill for months and we never worried about getting recognized before!

85
00:04:20,340 --> 00:04:23,260
Yeah, and we performed in the same stage as them back at Saga Rock!

86
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:25,980
Please, we can't go on without Ai after coming this far!

87
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:28,820
Froschuchu isn't Froschuchu if we're not singing together!

88
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:32,160
Respect my authority or you'll run laps till your legs fall off again!

89
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:34,740
As for you, we've got some solo gigs lined up.

90
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:36,740
You'll be starting first thing tomorrow.

91
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:38,000
At least!

92
00:04:40,740 --> 00:04:42,320
That didn't go too well.

93
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,080
So what now?

94
00:04:47,960 --> 00:04:49,900
There's no reasoning with that guy.

95
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:55,440
I'm sure one of us would have had to sit out eventually due to an injury or something like that.

96
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:59,880
Maybe this is an opportunity for each member of Froschuchu to get a bit stronger.

97
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:03,240
But it'll make me sad if you're the only person who's left out!

98
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:04,540
Well, it's just this once.

99
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:06,100
We want revenge, right?

100
00:05:06,260 --> 00:05:08,040
So we'll do whatever it takes to get it.

101
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:10,260
Junko?

102
00:05:10,740 --> 00:05:12,560
I'm counting on you to take charge.

103
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,740
After me, you're the most experienced idol we've got.

104
00:05:15,820 --> 00:05:16,260
Ugh.

105
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:19,840
Right!

106
00:05:19,840 --> 00:05:31,980
All right!

107
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:34,840
Today's special guest is number three from Froschuchu!

108
00:05:35,080 --> 00:05:35,340
Yay!

109
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:36,400
Woo!

110
00:05:36,860 --> 00:05:37,280
Hey!

111
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:39,240
I'm so happy to be here!

112
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:41,680
Huh?

113
00:05:42,460 --> 00:05:45,020
I guess number three's doing solo stuff these days.

114
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:47,480
I hope she's not breaking away from the gang.

115
00:05:47,840 --> 00:05:54,060
So I have to ask, has anyone ever told you that you bear a striking resemblance to the late Ai Mizuno from Iron Thrill?

116
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:57,680
Yes, I do get that from time to time, actually.

117
00:05:58,060 --> 00:06:00,840
She was a legendary idol who people still admire.

118
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:03,220
So I always consider it a compliment.

119
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:16,800
They want you in Fukuoka for a live event, plus the Nagasaki Hydrangea Festival, and Beppu Hot Springs Hell, too.

120
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:18,520
Now let me see here.

121
00:06:19,140 --> 00:06:21,720
Why don't you take those offers and shove them up, you buds?

122
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:22,800
What were you doing?

123
00:06:23,140 --> 00:06:25,960
Froschuchu was created for Saga and Saga alone.

124
00:06:26,320 --> 00:06:30,660
Anyone else who wants you is merely trying to capitalize on Saga's glory.

125
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,080
So trust no one.

126
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:34,680
I've never heard you say that before.

127
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:38,160
Are you plotting something?

128
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:43,520
Why would you want to split us up at such an important time?

129
00:06:44,740 --> 00:06:47,400
We can't afford to fail this next performance.

130
00:06:48,480 --> 00:06:49,860
Just think about it.

131
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:51,960
If it turns out like EFS did.

132
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:55,660
Oh, honey, Froschuchu can get along perfectly well without you.

133
00:06:56,300 --> 00:06:58,340
Besides, you left Junko in charge, right?

134
00:06:58,840 --> 00:06:59,520
What's wrong?

135
00:06:59,520 --> 00:07:00,640
You don't trust her?

136
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:05,420
Junko made it as a solo idol back in the 80s, when that was almost impossible to do.

137
00:07:05,860 --> 00:07:08,920
And they've all been working so hard to get over the EFS disaster.

138
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:10,940
I'm sure that they can pull through.

139
00:07:11,460 --> 00:07:13,460
It sounds like to me everything's pagey!

140
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:20,380
So if you just unclench your undead job for five minutes to focus on your solo career, and paying off this debt, we'd live happily ever after!

141
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:24,240
How am I supposed to do any of that if you keep on turning down offers for dumb reasons?

142
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:34,520
Everyone's been working so hard to learn the new choreo.

143
00:07:34,520 --> 00:07:39,700
But we're nowhere near the level we should be if we want to impress the fans coming to see Iron Frill.

144
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:42,260
We just have to push ourselves.

145
00:07:42,260 --> 00:07:47,360
The concert will be here before we know it.

146
00:07:47,360 --> 00:07:50,580
If we don't nail this performance, we're going to bomb again!

147
00:07:51,820 --> 00:07:52,300
Junko?

148
00:07:53,040 --> 00:07:54,140
Uh, Junko?

149
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:54,880
Uh...

150
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:56,840
Did we do better that time?

151
00:07:56,980 --> 00:07:59,640
I feel like we're still a little too stiff in some parts.

152
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:04,180
We should definitely go over it a couple more times, but you guys are doing a great job.

153
00:08:04,320 --> 00:08:05,240
Hell yeah! Rock!

154
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:09,600
You just stared at us all creepy with your mouth open, so I wasn't sure how you felt about it.

155
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:12,540
This concert is a big deal for Franshu Shuu!

156
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:15,140
We've got this, man! We've got this by the ass!

157
00:08:16,220 --> 00:08:20,240
Let's focus on one thing at a time before we start getting too excited, okay, ladies?

158
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:24,200
Yeah, I keep flailing my arms too much, and it's knocking my mic loose.

159
00:08:24,220 --> 00:08:27,660
That's because you're forgetting the choreo and making up your own dance moves.

160
00:08:27,660 --> 00:08:30,700
You seem troubled by something.

161
00:08:32,160 --> 00:08:34,260
I don't think you should be doing this right now.

162
00:08:34,900 --> 00:08:36,300
I'm so sorry, sir!

163
00:08:37,060 --> 00:08:38,500
Maybe you should call it a day.

164
00:08:57,660 --> 00:08:58,540
I'm back!

165
00:09:01,620 --> 00:09:02,800
Oh, hey there, Tai.

166
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:05,320
Is everyone else still off at work?

167
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:09,220
Up next is Franshu Shuu's number three singing Awaken Returner.

168
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:33,720
If she'd been alive during my time in the 80s, I bet she could have become a top idol, maybe even as a solo artist.

169
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:38,880
I have got to get out of this funk.

170
00:09:38,880 --> 00:09:54,920
Would you like to share your thoughts on the Saga Arena concert that's coming up this weekend?

171
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:58,700
Of course! We think it's gonna be a super incredible show!

172
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:04,920
Your national tour has generated a lot of buzz. People call you the top idol queens. Do you think you live up to the hype?

173
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:13,480
I mean, it would be conceded to say we're the best idols, but we're trendsetters, so we have a responsibility to keep evolving musically.

174
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:14,240
Shuri!

175
00:10:14,900 --> 00:10:17,840
Saga's a big deal to us, and we're gonna bring it on.

176
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:22,540
Iron Frill is gonna prove to everyone that we're one of a kind and beyond compare.

177
00:10:22,540 --> 00:10:26,780
We're better than ever, so get ready to see an amazing performance.

178
00:10:30,780 --> 00:10:36,160
Now that's a star right there. It seems like the top idols from Tokyo really know what they're doing, huh?

179
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:39,640
Isn't Franshu Shuu performing with them over at the new Saga Arena?

180
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:45,140
Yeah, they're the opening act. It'd be amazing if they managed to outperform Iron Frill.

181
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:47,360
I wouldn't place bets on that happening.

182
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:52,840
Hold on, did she just say they're one of a kind and beyond compare?

183
00:10:53,060 --> 00:10:56,480
So she's basically insulting the opening act as a declaration of war!

184
00:10:56,600 --> 00:10:58,220
I'll make her choke on those words!

185
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:00,160
Kinda doubt she knows us.

186
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:05,020
Iron Frill is an absurdly famous idol group. It's natural for them to be confident.

187
00:11:05,940 --> 00:11:10,060
If Iron Frill brings their A-game as promised, and if they perform on another level,

188
00:11:10,620 --> 00:11:15,900
people will think we're nothing more than third-rate wannabes, and we'll never be able to get our revenge.

189
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:27,780
This is how you type.

190
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:31,900
That's not right!

191
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:34,840
What do I do?

192
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:48,840
Sorry, guys. I had to work late today, and...

193
00:11:48,840 --> 00:11:50,840
this is how they feel better.

194
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:54,680
So, I dream time...

195
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:11,440
Go!

196
00:12:11,440 --> 00:12:18,680
Saga!

197
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:22,980
Did you like that?

198
00:12:23,440 --> 00:12:25,460
Did I like what?

199
00:12:25,640 --> 00:12:27,640
I thought our routine could use a little something extra

200
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:29,980
so we can go out with a bang at the Saga Arena.

201
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:32,180
Junko, check it out!

202
00:12:32,360 --> 00:12:34,100
Even Tai's getting into the groove.

203
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,320
Whoa, okay, but

204
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:42,620
we should probably be focusing on the song and dance moves first.

205
00:12:42,620 --> 00:12:44,260
Yeah, of course we'll do that too.

206
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:47,400
But there's not a whole lot of time left before the concert,

207
00:12:47,780 --> 00:12:49,480
so we thought we'd try something fresh

208
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:51,260
to leave a big impression on the audience.

209
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:53,700
It's bad enough without I being here,

210
00:12:54,180 --> 00:12:56,040
so we gotta dig ourselves out of this grave

211
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:58,020
or we'll have another disaster on our hands.

212
00:12:59,540 --> 00:13:00,340
What's wrong?

213
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:03,180
Does the routine need something extra?

214
00:13:04,220 --> 00:13:05,680
It's not that exactly.

215
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:08,260
Awesome, so you want in on this party?

216
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:13,240
I just need some more time to think about it.

217
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:14,820
You do that.

218
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:16,740
Okay, well try it again,

219
00:13:16,820 --> 00:13:18,300
but this time do it way louder.

220
00:13:18,620 --> 00:13:19,020
Yeah!

221
00:13:19,780 --> 00:13:22,460
I'm gonna shake these maracas like there's new tomorrow!

222
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:23,520
That's the spirit!

223
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:24,760
I'll do it too much!

224
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:32,760
I lost my Father'sви.

225
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:38,580
I know I can't believe in the money that I'm part of the night Thinkina.

226
00:13:38,780 --> 00:13:42,360
Will you return to what?

227
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:47,400
That's it, you're asking.

228
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:54,680
Please respond.

229
00:13:54,760 --> 00:14:18,520
There was an absolute love back home.

230
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:21,940
They were amorized she started dark.

231
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:28,940
NURURUR 박물

232
00:14:40,700 --> 00:14:42,480
Joongko, that was beautiful!

233
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:43,260
Did you write-

234
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:45,160
Ugh-

235
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:46,220
AHHHHHH!

236
00:14:46,220 --> 00:14:47,160
Oh… no

237
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:49,820
Ugh

238
00:14:49,820 --> 00:15:04,880
I've heard that song used in a bunch of commercials before, but I didn't know it was one of yours.

239
00:15:04,880 --> 00:15:10,620
Mm-hmm. It was the first one of my songs that managed to reach the top of the charts.

240
00:15:11,380 --> 00:15:16,200
It kept growing in popularity, and before long, everyone knew the name Junko Kono.

241
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:19,740
I like to sing it when I'm trying to cheer myself up.

242
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:22,340
I'm so sorry, Junko.

243
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:23,040
Huh?

244
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:29,600
I think maybe we're all in a state of panic right now. We're just too focused on having an impact.

245
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:38,280
Agreed. I feel the same way. We're all having anxiety about this show, but I thought it was only me that was feeling it.

246
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:45,440
I love being a part of this group, and I want us to put on a great performance at the Saga Arena.

247
00:15:46,300 --> 00:15:52,560
It's just, I'm so used to doing my own thing. Performing as a solo idol, you know?

248
00:15:54,860 --> 00:16:00,660
Performing with others is a totally different experience. You have to stand out and blend in at the same time.

249
00:16:00,660 --> 00:16:05,780
On top of that, I'm feeling everybody as a substitute idol leader.

250
00:16:07,980 --> 00:16:08,900
Not true!

251
00:16:09,400 --> 00:16:15,000
I happen to like your teaching methods because they're easy to understand, and you're super considerate of all of us.

252
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:17,720
You've schooled us on what it takes to be real idols.

253
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:19,260
You think so?

254
00:16:19,260 --> 00:16:27,420
Let's talk to Ai about this. She might have some good advice, even if she won't be able to be on stage with us.

255
00:16:27,900 --> 00:16:31,560
I know she's gone, but Kotaro never said we couldn't reach out to her.

256
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:32,840
You're right.

257
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:37,120
We'll tell her about our new ideas, and then we can pick her brain for some keen insight.

258
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:47,920
You're Fran Shishu's number three, right?

259
00:16:50,980 --> 00:16:52,700
And you're from Mayan Frill.

260
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:56,100
Wow, you really do look like her.

261
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:03,120
Hold on, is that Ai?

262
00:17:03,540 --> 00:17:04,980
And isn't that...

263
00:17:04,980 --> 00:17:13,380
I've been keeping a close eye on Fran Shishu for a good while now, so I know what happened at the EFS show.

264
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:17,040
But you've been doing solo gigs lately.

265
00:17:17,780 --> 00:17:19,560
I guess you've finally figured it out.

266
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:21,420
What do you mean by that?

267
00:17:21,780 --> 00:17:23,180
Just drop the dumb act.

268
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:26,220
You know you're more talented than those other girls are.

269
00:17:26,220 --> 00:17:31,360
I can tell by the way that you perform.

270
00:17:31,360 --> 00:17:34,920
You would rather be a part of a group as good as Iron Frill.

271
00:17:35,240 --> 00:17:37,060
I mean, why wouldn't you want to be?

272
00:17:37,380 --> 00:17:38,100
We're the ultimate.

273
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:39,980
The top idol queens.

274
00:17:41,980 --> 00:17:44,920
You may not want to admit it, but I see right through you.

275
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:47,440
Because I was also in a similar situation.

276
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,580
Ai Mizuno was an absolute legend as number one.

277
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:56,160
It hasn't been easy, but I've done everything in my power to shine brighter than she ever had the chance to.

278
00:17:56,160 --> 00:17:59,160
I'm just...

279
00:17:59,160 --> 00:18:00,860
Listen up, number three.

280
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:02,640
You should join Iron Frill.

281
00:18:05,140 --> 00:18:08,280
I think you've got what it takes.

282
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:13,060
And you'll be doing yourself a disservice if you don't leave a backwards place like Saga soon.

283
00:18:13,820 --> 00:18:15,900
You know Iron Frill is unbeatable.

284
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:19,520
Plus, we have the talent and the determination to stay on top, too.

285
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:22,100
You belong with our group, Ai.

286
00:18:22,320 --> 00:18:24,340
You're leagues ahead of Fran Shishu.

287
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:29,500
Just think about it, okay?

288
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:31,980
We'll talk again after the show this weekend.

289
00:18:33,820 --> 00:18:34,980
But you'll see.

290
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:40,500
Once you get a real taste of what we can do on stage, it'll be clear who the better group is.

291
00:18:40,500 --> 00:18:42,040
Oh, my God.

292
00:18:46,040 --> 00:18:47,560
Oh, my God.

293
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:52,020
Oh, my God.

294
00:18:52,020 --> 00:18:53,280
Oh, my God.

295
00:18:54,340 --> 00:18:55,660
Oh, my God.

296
00:18:55,780 --> 00:18:56,080
Oh, my God.

